- If the cpp framework itself binds the same endpoint twice (e.g. re-bind on lifecycle restart before unbind completed) → fix that owner.
- If Core refuses a rebind that the public contract allows (same context, after close/unbind returned; or after the old process exited) → STOP with a public C-API sequence.
